Explanation:
- The primary and secondary structures interact with each other (e.g., the secondary structure is attached to the primary structure). They also interact with the payload, power system, communication system, and attitude determination and control system because these components are typically mounted on or connected to the structures.
- The payload interacts with the power system for its operation, with the communication system to send data back to Earth, and with the attitude determination and control system to maintain its orientation.
- The power system provides energy to all other systems, so it has interactions with them.
